  "notes": "Per the 2026-2027 Texas A&M University undergraduate catalog: Supply Chain Management (BBA). Prerequisites are not listed in the catalog's plan of study grid; consult course descriptions.\nCatalog footnotes:\n[grid1 fn1] Refer to the specific major notes below for variations from the Business (lower level) requirements.\n[grid1 fn2] MATH 148 , MATH 152 , MATH 168 and MATH 172 will be accepted in lieu of MATH 140 .\n[grid1 fn3] For those students under ROTC contract, see Requirement 7 of the \"Requirements for a Baccalaureate Degree.\"\n[grid1 fn4] MATH 147 , MATH 151 and MATH 171 will be accepted in lieu of MATH 142 .\n[grid1 fn5] STAT 211 will be accepted in lieu of BUSN 203 .\n[grid2 fn1] This course is an approved writing-designated (W) or oral communication (C) business course. See your academic advisor for additional information.\n[grid2 fn2] For those students under ROTC contract, see Requirement 7 of the 'Requirements for a Baccalaureate Degree'.\n[grid2 fn3] Select in consultation with a supply chain management academic advisor. A list of acceptable courses is available in the department academic advising office.\n[grid2 fn4] A complete list of approved courses is available in the Undergraduate Advising Office. Three of the six required hours simultaneously fulfill the university's International and Cultural Diversity Graduation requirement.\n[grid2 fn5] Elective courses are open to any course offered for university credit, except ACCT 209 , ACCT 210 , FINC 409 , IBUS 301 , ISTM 209 , MGMT 209 , MGMT 309 , MKTG 409 , SCMT 309 . Additional restrictions may apply; see academic advisor for information. May be taken on a satisfactory/unsatisfactory basis.",
